# gtools/tables.golfj — the code page and the template blob, built from the
# source data in GOLF.
#
# The GOLF twin of tools/mkblob2.py, tools/mktables.py and tools/codepage.py's
# table/reference/check: everything those build from data/ops.tsv and
# data/templates.txt, this builds too, and test/gtools.sh requires every output
# to be byte-identical to the Python's, on the real repo files.
#
#     build/gtables COMMAND          (run from expanded/; output on stdout)
#
#   blob        the template blob, raw (mkblob2.build_blob2())
#   escape      the blob as the ` escape both compilers embed (blob_escape())
#   blobhex     data/blob.hex                       (mktables.py)
#   codepage    data/codepage.tsv                   (mktables.py)
#   seed        self/seed.golf                      (mkblob2.build_seed())
#   golf2       self/golf2.golf                     (mkblob2.build_golf2())
#   table       `codepage.py table`
#   reference   `codepage.py reference`, the REFERENCE.md generated block
#   check       `codepage.py check`: silent, exit 0; or the report on fd 2, exit 1
#
# It reads data/ops.tsv, data/templates.txt and data/v1.hex (and
# self/seed.golfv1, self/golf2.golfj, lib/prelude.golfj for the commands that
# need them), from the working directory.  Every command loads and expands all
# three tables first, as importing mkblob2 does, so a broken table stops every
# command with the same message the Python gives: `data/ops.tsv:12: …` or
# `data/templates.txt:40: …` on fd 2, exit 1, nothing on stdout.  The output is
# built in one vector and written once at the end, so a failure part-way leaves
# stdout empty.
#
# The template notation is documented at the top of data/templates.txt; the
# expander below follows tools/mkblob2.Templates step for step (same checks,
# same order, same messages), so the two can be diffed on bad input as well as
# good.
#
# Written in the prelude's own vocabulary (code lists, ‹dict›, ‹vec›, ⊡
# locals) rather than the raw style of the older gtools: it uses no fixed
# cell, no one-byte word and nothing from lib/t*.golfj.  Every word is a
# ‹tl_…› long name; the globals are long-name variables.

# ============================================================ small words
:‹tl_eq›≣1+;                                   # a b -> 0 when structurally equal
:‹tl_hd›"10<1+[48+⋄55+];                       # 0..15 -> its uppercase hex digit
⊡‹tl_hx2›⇒n‹vec›⇐n 4>15$‹tl_hd›⍆⇐n 15$‹tl_hd›⍆;   # n -> “HH“
⊡‹tl_cat›⇒l⇒v 0⇒i{⇐i⇐l≢<1+⋄⇐v⇐l⇐i⊇⍆⇒v⇡i}⇐v;      # v l -> v' (l appended)
⊡‹tl_le4›⇒x‹vec›⇒o 0⇒k{⇐k 4<1+⋄⇐o⇐x⇐k 8*≫255$⍆⇒o⇡k}⇐o;   # x -> 4 bytes LE
⊡‹tl_each›⇒f⇒l 0⇒i{⇐i⇐l≢<1+⋄⇐l⇐i⊇⇐f⍎⇡i};       # l ′f -> (f on each)
:‹tl_q›“'“⊃\\⧺“'“⊃⧺;                           # s -> 's'

# The output: one vector, written at the very end.
:‹tl_b›←‹o›\\⍆→‹o›;                            # b ->
:‹tl_s›←‹o›\\‹tl_cat›→‹o›;                     # list ->
:‹tl_z›⊃‹tl_s›;                                # “…“ ->

# Failure: the message and a newline on fd 2, exit 1.  Nothing has been
# printed yet (the output vector is written last), so stdout stays empty.
:‹tl_die›10⍆2‹fwrite›1.;                       # msg ->
⊡‹tl_ldie›⇒m⇒n⇒f⇐f“:“⊃⧺⇐n‹fmt›⧺“: “⊃⧺⇐m⧺‹tl_die›;   # file line msg ->
⊡‹tl_opsdie›⇒m⇒n“data/ops.tsv“⊃⇐n⇐m‹tl_ldie›;           # line msg ->
⊡‹tl_tdie›⇒m⇒n“data/templates.txt“⊃⇐n⇐m‹tl_ldie›;      # line msg ->

# Character classes.  Each answers 0 for yes (zero-is-true, like [ and ∊).
⊡‹tl_rng›⇒h⇒l⇒c⇐c⇐l≺⇐h⇐c≺|;                    # c lo hi -> 0 if lo <= c <= hi
⊡‹tl_isuhex›⇒c⇐c 48 57‹tl_rng›⇐c 65 70‹tl_rng›$;
⊡‹tl_ishex›⇒c⇐c‹tl_isuhex›⇐c 97 102‹tl_rng›$;
⊡‹tl_isdig›⇒c⇐c 48 57‹tl_rng›;
⊡‹tl_isalpha›⇒c⇐c 65 90‹tl_rng›⇐c 97 122‹tl_rng›$;
⊡‹tl_isidc›⇒c⇐c‹tl_isalpha›⇐c‹tl_isdig›$⇐c 95-$;
⊡‹tl_isws›⇒c⇐c 9 13‹tl_rng›⇐c 28 32‹tl_rng›$;   # Python's ASCII \s
⊡‹tl_all›⇒f⇒l 0⇒r 0⇒i{⇐i⇐l≢<1+⋄⇐l⇐i⊇⇐f⍎[⋄1⇒r]⇡i}⇐r;   # l ′f -> 0 if f says 0 for all
⊡‹tl_isid›⇒s⇐s≢[1^]⇐s 0⊇‹tl_isalpha›⇐s 0⊇95-$[⋄1^]⇐s′‹tl_isidc›‹tl_all›;
:‹tl_notid›‹tl_isid›[1⋄0];
⊡‹tl_ishexs›⇒s⇐s≢[1^]⇐s′‹tl_ishex›‹tl_all›;   # nonempty, all hex
⊡‹tl_isdigs›⇒s⇐s≢[1^]⇐s′‹tl_isdig›‹tl_all›;   # nonempty, all decimal
:‹tl_isbyte›"≢2-[‹tl_ishexs›⋄_1];              # exactly two hex digits
⊡‹tl_get›⇒i⇒s⇐i⇐s≢<1+[⇐s⇐i⊇⋄0 1-];        # s i -> s[i], or -1 past the end
⊡‹tl_skipto›⇒c⇒i⇒s{⇐s⇐i‹tl_get›"⇐c-\\1+*0≡⋄⇡i}⇐i;   # s i c -> index of the next c, or the end
⊡‹tl_ncp›⇒s 0⇒n 0⇒i{⇐i⇐s≢<1+⋄⇐s⇐i⊇128 191‹tl_rng›[⋄⇡n]⇡i}⇐n;   # UTF-8 code points

# Substrings.  ‹tl_at›: 0 if p occurs in h at i.  ‹tl_find›: the first
# occurrence at or after i, or -1.
⊡‹tl_at›⇒i⇒p⇒h⇐i⇐p≢+⇐h≢»1+[1^]0⇒k{⇐k⇐p≢<1+⋄⇐h⇐i⇐k+⊇⇐p⇐k⊇-[⋄1^]⇡k}0;
⊡‹tl_find›⇒i⇒p⇒h{⇐i⇐p≢+⇐h≢»⋄⇐h⇐p⇐i‹tl_at›[⇐i^]⇡i}0 1-;
⊡‹tl_count›⇒p⇒h 0⇒n 0⇒i{⇐h⇐p⇐i‹tl_find›"⇒i 0≺⋄⇡n⇐i⇐p≢+⇒i}⇐n;    # non-overlapping
⊡‹tl_repl›⇒r⇒p⇒h‹vec›⇒o 0⇒i 0⇒j
{⇐h⇐p⇐i‹tl_find›"⇒j 0≺⋄⇐o⇐h⇐i⇐j⇐i-‹slice›‹tl_cat›⇐r‹tl_cat›⇒o⇐j⇐p≢+⇒i}
⇐o⇐h⇐i↓‹tl_cat›;                                # h p r -> h with every p made r

# ============================================================ data/ops.tsv
# ‹ops› is a vector of rows [table byte mnemonic glyph doc], table being the
# letter's code (65 A, 67 C, 76 L), in file order.  Only the SHAPE is
# checked here, as mkblob2.read_ops does; the namespace rules are `check`'s.
⊡‹tl_row›⇒n⇒s⇐s 9‹split›⇒f
⇐f≢5-[⋄⇐n“expected 5 TAB-separated fields, found “⊃⇐f≢‹fmt›⧺‹tl_opsdie›]
⇐f 0⊇⇒t⇐f 1⊇⇒b⇐f 2⊇⇒m⇐f 3⊇⇒g
⇐t≢1-[⇐t 0⊇⋄0]⇒c
⇐c 65-⇐c 67-*⇐c 76-*[⋄⇐n“table must be A, C or L, not “⊃⇐t‹tl_q›⧺‹tl_opsdie›]
⇐b≢2-[⇐b′‹tl_isuhex›‹tl_all›⋄1][⋄⇐n“byte must be two uppercase hex digits, not “⊃⇐b‹tl_q›⧺‹tl_opsdie›]
⇐m≢[1⋄⇐m′‹tl_isalpha›‹tl_all›][⋄⇐n“mnemonic must be ASCII letters, not “⊃⇐m‹tl_q›⧺‹tl_opsdie›]
⇐g‹tl_ncp›1-[⋄⇐n“glyph must be one character, not “⊃⇐g‹tl_q›⧺‹tl_opsdie›]
‹vec›⇐c⍆⇐b‹parsehex›⍆⇐m⍆⇐g⍆⇐f 4⊇⍆;
⊡‹tl_ops›“data/ops.tsv“⊃‹readfile›10‹split›⇒l‹vec›⇒v 0⇒i
{⇐i⇐l≢<1+⋄⇐l⇐i⊇⇒s⇡i⇐s≢[⋄⇐s 0⊇35-[⋄⇐v⇐s⇐i‹tl_row›⍆⇒v]]}⇐v→‹ops›;
⊡‹tl_rows›⇒c‹vec›⇒v 0⇒i{⇐i←‹ops›≢<1+⋄←‹ops›⇐i⊇⇒r⇐r 0⊇⇐c-[⇐v⇐r⍆⇒v]⇡i}⇐v;   # one table

# ============================================================ data/v1.hex
# ‹v1r›: key -> template bytes, every record; ‹v1o›: the keys > 5 in file
# order, which is the order `v1ops` emits them in (v1.TEMPLATES).
⊡‹tl_v1›“data/v1.hex“⊃‹readfile›10‹split›⇒l‹dict›→‹v1r›‹vec›⇒o 0⇒i
{⇐i⇐l≢<1+⋄⇐l⇐i⊇‹trim›⇒s⇡i⇐s≢[⋄⇐s 0⊇35-[⋄
⇐s‹words›′‹parsehex›€⇒b⇐b 0⊇⇒k⇐b 2↓⇒d
⇐b 1⊇⇐d≢-[⋄“v1.hex: record “⊃⇐k‹fmt›⧺“ claims “⊃⧺⇐b 1⊇‹fmt›⧺“, has “⊃⧺⇐d≢‹fmt›⧺‹tl_die›]
←‹v1r›⇐k⇐d‹put›_⇐k 5»1+[⇐o⇐k⍆⇒o]]]}⇐o→‹v1o›;

# ============================================================ data/templates.txt
# Parsed into ‹defs› (name -> [params tokens line]), ‹tpls› and ‹ovs› (byte
# -> [tokens line]; ‹ovo› keeps the override bytes in file order) and ‹sts›,
# the emission statements [kind key tokens line] in order, kind being 114 rec,
# 118 v1ops, 97 atoms.  A statement's tokens are collected over its indented
# lines and stored when the next statement (or the end of the file) closes
# it: ‹ck› is the open statement's kind (0 none, 100 def, 114 rec, 116 tpl,
# 111 override), ‹cn› its name or byte, ‹cp› a def's parameters, ‹ct› the
# tokens, ‹cl› its line.
:‹tl_fin›
←‹ck›100-[←‹defs›←‹cn›‹vec›←‹cp›⍆←‹ct›⍆←‹cl›⍆‹put›_]
←‹ck›114-[←‹sts›‹vec›114⍆←‹cn›⍆←‹ct›⍆←‹cl›⍆⍆→‹sts›]
←‹ck›116-[←‹tpls›←‹cn›‹vec›←‹ct›⍆←‹cl›⍆‹put›_]
←‹ck›111-[←‹ovs›←‹cn›‹vec›←‹ct›⍆←‹cl›⍆‹put›_←‹ovo›←‹cn›⍆→‹ovo›]
0→‹ck›;
⊡‹tl_iskw›⇒k⇐k“def“⊃‹tl_eq›⇐k“rec“⊃‹tl_eq›$⇐k“tpl“⊃‹tl_eq›$⇐k“override“⊃‹tl_eq›$
⇐k“v1ops“⊃‹tl_eq›$⇐k“atoms“⊃‹tl_eq›$;
⊡‹tl_stmt›⇒n⇒t⇐t 0⊇⇒k⇐t 1↓⇒a
⇐k‹tl_iskw›[⋄⇐n“unknown statement “⊃⇐k‹tl_q›⧺‹tl_tdie›]
⇐k“v1ops“⊃‹tl_eq›⇐k“atoms“⊃‹tl_eq›$[
 ⇐a≢[⋄⇐n⇐k“ takes nothing“⊃⧺‹tl_tdie›]
 ←‹sts›‹vec›⇐k 0⊇⍆0⍆‹vec›⍆⇐n⍆⍆→‹sts›^]
⇐a≢[⇐n⇐k“ needs a “⊃⧺⇐k“def“⊃‹tl_eq›[“name“⋄“byte“]⊃⧺‹tl_tdie›]
⇐k“def“⊃‹tl_eq›[
 ⇐a′‹tl_notid›⍷⇒i⇐i 0≺[⇐n“bad fragment or parameter name “⊃⇐a⇐i⊇‹tl_q›⧺‹tl_tdie›]
 ←‹defs›⇐a 0⊇‹has›[⇐n“fragment “⊃⇐a 0⊇⧺“ defined twice“⊃⧺‹tl_tdie›]
 100→‹ck›⇐a 0⊇→‹cn›⇐a 1↓→‹cp›‹vec›→‹ct›⇐n→‹cl›^]
⇐a 0⊇‹tl_isbyte›[⋄⇐n“expected a two-digit hex byte, not “⊃⇐a 0⊇‹tl_q›⧺‹tl_tdie›]
⇐a 0⊇‹parsehex›⇒b
⇐k“rec“⊃‹tl_eq›[114⋄
 ⇐k“tpl“⊃‹tl_eq›[←‹tpls›⋄←‹ovs›]⇐b‹has›[⇐n⇐k“ “⊃⧺⇐b‹tl_hx2›⧺“ given twice“⊃⧺‹tl_tdie›]
 ⇐k“tpl“⊃‹tl_eq›[116⋄111]]→‹ck›
⇐b→‹cn›‹vec›⇐a 1↓‹tl_cat›→‹ct›⇐n→‹cl›;
⊡‹tl_tparse›“data/templates.txt“⊃‹readfile›10‹split›⇒l 0⇒i
‹dict›→‹defs›‹dict›→‹tpls›‹dict›→‹ovs›‹vec›→‹ovo›‹vec›→‹sts›0→‹ck›‹dict›→‹nod›
{⇐i⇐l≢<1+⋄⇐l⇐i⊇⇒r⇡i
 ⇐r 35‹indexof›⇒j⇐j 0≺1+[⇐r⋄⇐r 0⇐j‹slice›]‹words›⇒t
 ⇐t≢[⋄⇐r 0⊇32-⇐r 0⊇9-*[
  ←‹ck›[⇐i“an indented line with no statement above it“⊃‹tl_tdie›]←‹ct›⇐t‹tl_cat›→‹ct›⋄
  ‹tl_fin›⇐t⇐i‹tl_stmt›]]}
‹tl_fin›;

# ------------------------------------------------------------ expansion
# ‹tl_body›: tokens env line depth -> bytes.  Labels are this body's own; a
# jump is a placeholder of 1 or 4 zero bytes, filled once every label of the
# body is known.  ‹tl_tok› expands one token, ‹tl_call› one fragment.
⊡‹tl_body›⇒d⇒n⇒e⇒t
⇐d 32»1+[⇐n“fragments nest more than 32 deep (a cycle?)“⊃‹tl_tdie›]
‹vec›⇒o‹dict›⇒b‹vec›⇒j 0⇒i
{⇐i⇐t≢<1+⋄⇐t⇐i⊇⇒s⇡i
 ⇐s‹last›58-[⇐s"≢1-↑‹tl_isid›⋄1]
 [⇐s"≢1-↑⇒q⇐b⇐q‹has›[⇐n“label “⊃⇐q⧺“ defined twice in one body“⊃⧺‹tl_tdie›]⇐b⇐q⇐o≢‹put›_⋄
 ⇐s 0⊇62-[
  ⇐s“>>“⊃‹startswith›[4⋄1]⇒w⇐s⇐w 1-[1⋄2]↓⇒q
  ⇐q‹tl_isid›[⋄⇐n“bad jump “⊃⇐s‹tl_q›⧺‹tl_tdie›]
  ⇐j‹vec›⇐o≢⍆⇐w⍆⇐q⍆⍆⇒j 0⇒k{⇐k⇐w<1+⋄⇐o 0⍆⇒o⇡k}⋄
  ⇐o⇐s⇐e⇐n⇐d‹tl_tok›‹tl_cat›⇒o]]}
0⇒i{⇐i⇐j≢<1+⋄⇐j⇐i⊇⇒s⇡i⇐s 0⊇⇒p⇐s 1⊇⇒w⇐s 2⊇⇒q
 ⇐b⇐q‹has›[⋄⇐n“jump to undefined label “⊃⇐q⧺‹tl_tdie›]
 ⇐b⇐q‹get›⇐p⇐w+-⇒x
 ⇐w 1-[⇐x 0 128-≺⇐x 127≻|[⋄⇐n“jump to “⊃⇐q⧺“ is “⊃⧺⇐x‹fmt›⧺“ bytes, out of rel8 range“⊃⧺‹tl_tdie›]]
 0⇒k{⇐k⇐w<1+⋄⇐o⇐p⇐k+⇐x⇐k 8*≫255$⍈⇒o⇡k}}
⇐o;

⊡‹tl_call›⇒d⇒n⇒a⇒m
←‹defs›⇐m‹has›[⋄⇐n“no fragment named “⊃⇐m⧺‹tl_tdie›]
←‹defs›⇐m‹get›⇒x⇐x 0⊇⇒p
⇐a≢⇐p≢-[⋄⇐n⇐m“ takes “⊃⧺⇐p≢‹fmt›⧺“ argument(s), given “⊃⧺⇐a≢‹fmt›⧺‹tl_tdie›]
‹dict›⇒e 0⇒i{⇐i⇐p≢<1+⋄⇐e⇐p⇐i⊇⇐a⇐i⊇‹put›_⇡i}
⇐x 1⊇⇐e⇐x 2⊇⇐d‹tl_body›;

# One token -> its bytes, trying the forms in mkblob2.Templates.token's order.
⊡‹tl_tok›⇒d⇒n⇒e⇒s
⇐s≢[⇐n“cannot read token ''“⊃‹tl_tdie›]
⇐s‹tl_isbyte›[‹vec›⇐s‹parsehex›⍆^]
⇐s“w:“⊃‹startswith›[⇐s 2↓⇒q⇐q‹tl_ishexs›⇐q≢8»|[⇐q‹parsehex›‹tl_le4›^]]
⇐s 0⊇36-[⇐s 1↓⇒q⇐e⇐q‹has›[⇐e⇐q‹get›^]⇐n⇐s“ is not a parameter here“⊃⧺‹tl_tdie›]
⇐s“v1:“⊃‹startswith›[⇐s 3↓⇒q⇐q 2↑⇒h⇐q 2↓⇒r
 ⇐h‹tl_isbyte›⇐r≢[0⋄⇐r 0⊇43-⇐r 1↓‹tl_isdigs›|]|[
  ⇐h‹parsehex›⇒k←‹v1r›⇐k‹has›[⋄⇐n“data/v1.hex has no record “⊃⇐k‹tl_hx2›⧺‹tl_tdie›]
  ←‹v1r›⇐k‹get›⇐r≢[0⋄⇐r 1↓‹num›]↓^]]
⇐s“atom:“⊃‹startswith›[⇐s 5↓⇒q⇐q‹tl_isbyte›[
 ⇐q‹parsehex›⇒k←‹tpls›⇐k‹has›[⋄⇐n“no `tpl “⊃⇐k‹tl_hx2›⧺“`“⊃⧺‹tl_tdie›]
 ←‹tpls›⇐k‹get›⇒x⇐x 0⊇←‹nod›⇐x 1⊇⇐d 1+‹tl_body›^]]
⇐s“len:“⊃‹startswith›[⇐s 4↓⇒q⇐q‹tl_isid›[
 ⇐q‹vec›⇐n⇐d 1+‹tl_call›≢⇒k
 ⇐k 255»1+[⇐n“len:“⊃⇐q⧺“ is “⊃⧺⇐k‹fmt›⧺“, more than a byte“⊃⧺‹tl_tdie›]
 ‹vec›⇐k⍆^]]
⇐s 40‹indexof›⇒p
⇐p 0≺1+[⇐s‹tl_isid›[⇐s‹vec›⇐n⇐d 1+‹tl_call›^]⋄
 ⇐s 0⇐p‹slice›⇒q⇐s⇐p 1+⇐s≢⇐p-2-‹slice›⇒r
